00:04:04.277 --> 00:04:05.478
But that thing,
like, that thing,

00:04:05.478 --> 00:04:08.014 align:start size:97% position:3%
the struggle to the success-
- Yeah.

00:04:08.014 --> 00:04:09.448
- Tell me, I know your story,

00:04:09.448 --> 00:04:10.717
but can you gimme,
like, the brief,

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:11.951
like, struggle-to-success story?

00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:13.753 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah, I mean, you talk
about tuna, you know.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.389
When I was in the army,
I would get the tuna

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.557 align:start size:88% position:13%
'cause it was disgusting
but the can was,

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.993 align:start size:84% position:16%
like, 49 cents at PX,
(David laughing)

00:04:20.993 --> 00:04:22.728
and you would mix
it with mustard

00:04:22.728 --> 00:04:24.897
'cause at least mustard
would make it tolerable.

00:04:24.897 --> 00:04:26.332
And throughout the day,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.168 align:start size:97% position:3%
I would have 3, 4, 5 of these
cans to get the protein.

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, listen, regular-
- Hey, tuna, tuna might be

00:04:31.304 --> 00:04:32.305
the key to the whole operation.

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.539
- I think that's what it is.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.741
Mercury, we're both
gonna go through,

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.375
one day news is gonna come out.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:39.044 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Dave Rubin and
Patrick Bet-David are
dealing with mercury,

00:04:39.044 --> 00:04:41.647
having too much of it," but
no, I mean, look, you know,

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:43.182
it all starts with a dream.

00:04:43.182 --> 00:04:45.017
I was talking to a couple
of the guys the other day.

00:04:45.017 --> 00:04:46.786 align:start size:97% position:3%
Just yesterday, we were doing
a Zoom call with a couple

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:50.155
of our executives, and
one of my guys says,

00:04:50.155 --> 00:04:53.158
"Hey, one of my sales
guys I'm dealing with,

00:04:53.158 --> 00:04:54.827 align:start size:84% position:16%
he's very difficult
to deal with.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:57.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a pain in the ass,
and he's tough to do this,

00:04:57.396 --> 00:04:58.331
and da, da, da, da, da."

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.199
He's a 1099 guy, not W-2.

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:02.534 align:start size:88% position:13%
W-2, you have the option
to fire, and coach,

00:05:02.534 --> 00:05:03.936
and send him to places,

00:05:03.936 --> 00:05:06.205
but 1099, you're working
with these guys, right?

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:08.307 align:start size:88% position:13%
It's like you're running
a insurance office

00:05:08.307 --> 00:05:09.775
and real estate office.

00:05:09.775 --> 00:05:10.977
So he says, "What
do I do with them?"

00:05:10.977 --> 00:05:12.378
I said, well, "Let
me tell you what I do

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.379
in these types of situations."

00:05:14.379 --> 00:05:18.217
I said, "For a guy like me,
I joined the army at 18,

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:21.420
okay, April 15th, 1997."

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:25.892 align:start size:88% position:13%
I get shipped to Fort
Jackson, South Carolina.

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:27.260
My ASVAB score wasn't high,

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:29.262
so I only could be
infantry or mechanic.

00:05:29.262 --> 00:05:30.830
So I became a Hummer mechanic.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:32.231
I had 13 Hummers to myself.

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.933
I had a couple FMTVs and LMTVs.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:35.100
These are the bigger trucks.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:37.169 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I had a Hotel-8
certification,

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:40.673 align:start size:97% position:3%
which means I can go tow cars
out of the mud, you know,

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.309 align:start position:0%
trucks out of the mud, and
that's what I did for a living.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.945
I thought I was gonna
do 20 years, literally.

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.680
I'm gonna be in the
army for 20 years.

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.114
Then, I'm gonna get out.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:51.750 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna get an additional
10 points on my score

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:55.154 align:start size:97% position:3%
to be working at the post
office, or cop, or firefighter

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.556
because if you're
former military,

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:57.990 align:start size:84% position:16%
you get that 10
points on the test.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:05:59.758
So if somebody scored 75,

00:05:59.758 --> 00:06:01.327
but you're in the
army, you get 85.

00:06:01.327 --> 00:06:03.062
If you do 82, you do 92, right?

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.030
So I had that advantage.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.633
Then one day, I get a call
from a friend of mine, Kogan.

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:09.068
He says, "Hey, Pat,
what are you doing?"

00:06:09.068 --> 00:06:11.504 align:start size:97% position:3%
I said, "Tomorrow, I'm
reenlisting for six years."

00:06:11.504 --> 00:06:12.438
"Really?"

00:06:12.438 --> 00:06:13.705
"Yeah, I'm reenlisting tomorrow.

00:06:13.705 --> 00:06:15.141
They got me everything
I wanted on my orders.

00:06:15.141 --> 00:06:18.911 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'm gonna go special
forces, Delta, SERE school.

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.445
You know, I speak
five languages.

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:22.715
So they're gonna help me
out to sharpen my language.

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:24.183
And then I'm gonna
go to Vicenza, Italy,

00:06:24.183 --> 00:06:25.284
which is where I
wanted to go to.

00:06:25.284 --> 00:06:27.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
There was a
beautiful unit there.

00:06:27.153 --> 00:06:28.454
And then from there, you know,

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.189 align:start size:81% position:19%
I'm gonna to do
this for 20 years,

00:06:30.189 --> 00:06:32.391 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I'm gonna retire
at 38 years old,

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:34.059
and then I'm gonna go be
a cop and firefighter.

00:06:34.059 --> 00:06:35.027 align:start size:81% position:19%
He says, "Pat, you
gotta get out."

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:36.361
I said, "I'm not getting out.

00:06:36.361 --> 00:06:39.665
I'm signing my contract
tomorrow for six years,

00:06:39.665 --> 00:06:41.300
and I'm getting my Army
Commendation Medal."

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.635
I had gotten an Army
Achievement Medal.

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:44.136
Tomorrow was a celebration.

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:45.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
Lieutenant Colonel
Peacocks was gonna give me

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:47.440
an Army Commendation Medal.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:49.141 align:start size:88% position:13%
He says, "Can I
convince you otherwise?"

00:06:49.141 --> 00:06:50.376
I said, "You can."

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:53.713
My dad already sent me
a $250 camera as a gift

00:06:53.713 --> 00:06:55.748
for committing to reenlist.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:57.382
He says, "Just gimme an hour."

00:06:57.382 --> 00:06:59.351
And this guy was the only guy
that ever came and visited me

00:06:59.351 --> 00:07:00.886
in the army outta my
friends for 18 days.

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:02.088 align:start size:84% position:16%
And when you're in the
army, you're alone.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:03.355
You remember all the letters.

00:07:03.355 --> 00:07:05.925
I kept every letter,
every single letter

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:07.894 align:start size:88% position:13%
anybody ever wrote me
while I was in bootcamp.

00:07:07.894 --> 00:07:09.629 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have all of it till
today, all of it.

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.297 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you know, like,
who's a friend,

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.466
and who's thinking, and
who's not, all of 'em.

00:07:13.466 --> 00:07:14.934 align:start size:84% position:16%
The people you thought
they're your best,

00:07:14.934 --> 00:07:16.502
they never wrote you a letter.

00:07:16.502 --> 00:07:18.204 align:start size:97% position:3%
The people you thought
were, like, they were okay,

00:07:18.204 --> 00:07:19.839
they wrote you 50, 60 letters.

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:22.508 align:start size:81% position:19%
So I'm sitting
there, hour later.

00:07:22.508 --> 00:07:23.809
It's now 1:00 in the morning.

00:07:23.809 --> 00:07:25.310 align:start size:84% position:16%
I got formation
early in the morning.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:26.578
I can't sleep all night.

00:07:26.578 --> 00:07:28.180
I've already promised my
dad I'm gonna reenlist.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.148 align:start size:97% position:3%
He wants me to stay in
uniform, be in the military.

00:07:30.148 --> 00:07:32.485
I get out in the morning, go
to Lieutenant Colonel Peacocks.

00:07:32.485 --> 00:07:34.420
"Disappointing news for
you, I can't reenlist.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:35.521
I gotta get out."

00:07:35.521 --> 00:07:36.722
"Bet-David, what are you doing?

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.224
We got you the orders."

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:40.760
I said, "You have no clue
how much I respect you,

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:42.061 align:start size:84% position:16%
but I'm getting
out," so I get out.

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:44.096
They don't give me the
Army Commendation Medal.

00:07:44.096 --> 00:07:45.531
- How difficult were

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:46.798
those few hours?
- Wasn't easy.

00:07:46.798 --> 00:07:48.300
I mean, I'm thinking
about it right now.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.870
I'm going back because I threw
my boots over the, you know,

00:07:50.870 --> 00:07:53.573
you celebrate, like,
"Hey, this is it."

00:07:53.573 --> 00:07:54.740
It wasn't easy. Let me tell you.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.676
It was a lot of anxiety because,

00:07:56.676 --> 00:07:58.443 align:start size:97% position:3%
when you're in the military,
it's so regimented,

00:07:58.443 --> 00:08:01.180
it's so, like, routine,
and if you like routine,

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.916
there's a lot of trust
and comfort in routine.

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:05.718 align:start size:84% position:16%
There's order,
there's expectation,

00:08:05.718 --> 00:08:07.553
there's a time for formation.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.655
It's a lotta good things,
your benefits, chow hall,

00:08:09.655 --> 00:08:12.157
when you eat, how much you
get paid, your promotions,

00:08:12.157 --> 00:08:14.393
correspondence courses
you gotta take, you know,

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.228
you'll be an E-5, E-6, E-7.

00:08:16.228 --> 00:08:17.930
Eventually, you'll
be a drill sergeant,

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.465
maybe a, you know,
first sergeant, then
sergeant major, E-9.

00:08:20.465 --> 00:08:22.301
And that's kind of
the route you go.

00:08:22.301 --> 00:08:24.136 align:start size:84% position:16%
And you can take
advantage of GI Bill,

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.905 align:start size:88% position:13%
maybe become an officer,
a second lieutenant,

00:08:26.905 --> 00:08:28.340
first lieutenant,
work your way up.

00:08:28.340 --> 00:08:31.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
So there was an immediate,
and you can travel,

00:08:31.010 --> 00:08:31.978
see the world.

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:34.880
You know 20 years what
it's gonna look like.

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:36.381
It's predictable.

00:08:36.381 --> 00:08:38.350 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I like the
predictable aspect.

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:40.385
But I also have a
uncertainty aspect.

00:08:40.385 --> 00:08:41.854
The unknown fires me up.

00:08:41.854 --> 00:08:44.490 align:start size:88% position:13%
There's an element of
unknown that's exciting,

00:08:44.490 --> 00:08:45.825
that level of curiosity.

00:08:45.825 --> 00:08:48.127
I wanna know what the
possibilities are.

00:08:48.127 --> 00:08:50.029
So then, I get out.

00:08:50.029 --> 00:08:51.263
I get outta the military,

00:08:51.263 --> 00:08:52.531
I come out to be
a Hummer mechanic.

00:08:52.531 --> 00:08:55.067
And there was one
shop at Camarillo,

00:08:56.134 --> 00:08:57.536 align:start size:84% position:16%
and it was Thousand
Oaks, Camarillo

00:08:57.536 --> 00:08:59.372 align:start size:97% position:3%
that had a Hummer dealership,
so I go, and I said,

00:08:59.372 --> 00:09:00.673 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Listen, I'm the
best Hummer mechanic

00:09:00.673 --> 00:09:02.474
in Fort Campbell, Kentucky."

00:09:02.474 --> 00:09:04.143
And the guy says, "Listen
man, we sell maybe one

00:09:04.143 --> 00:09:05.778
or two Hummers a month, H1,

00:09:05.778 --> 00:09:07.179 align:start size:84% position:16%
we have one mechanic
if we're lucky.

00:09:07.179 --> 00:09:08.814
We don't need a second one."

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:10.282
And I said, "I'm very
good at shooting."

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:12.084
He says, "Listen, we don't
need a hitman here, you know.

00:09:12.084 --> 00:09:13.986
You're not gonna
use it in private."

00:09:13.986 --> 00:09:17.223
So at that point I went and
took the test to be a cop.

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:20.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had 16 speeding tickets,
so I couldn't be a cop.

00:09:20.293 --> 00:09:22.528 align:start size:84% position:16%
And then firefighter,
there was a hold.

00:09:22.528 --> 00:09:23.795 align:start size:81% position:19%
And then boom,
(fingers snapping)

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:25.331
five-year freeze on
being a firefighter.

00:09:25.331 --> 00:09:27.266
Then, I get out and
start making money

00:09:27.266 --> 00:09:30.469 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the financial sector,
Morgan Stanley, Transamerica.

00:09:30.469 --> 00:09:32.437
Then, I start my own
insurance company,

00:09:32.437 --> 00:09:33.705
and the rest is history.

00:09:33.705 --> 00:09:35.308
The point I was making
with this meeting was

00:09:35.308 --> 00:09:39.311 align:start size:81% position:19%
the level of grace
God has on us.

00:09:39.311 --> 00:09:41.547
When you go back and think
about the people you met

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:43.415
in your life, some of them were,

00:09:43.415 --> 00:09:45.417
they made such a big
impact in your life,

00:09:45.417 --> 00:09:47.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're a five-minute
person in your life.

00:09:47.886 --> 00:09:49.288
You're at Nordstrom's.

00:09:49.288 --> 00:09:51.356
Your son is wrestling with you.

00:09:51.356 --> 00:09:54.292
A woman over here who's 65
years old's looking at me

00:09:54.292 --> 00:09:57.163
for 10 minutes while me
and Dylan are wrestling.

00:09:57.163 --> 00:09:58.130
I said, "Ma'am, how you doing?"

00:09:58.130 --> 00:09:59.365
She said, "I'm doing good."

00:09:59.365 --> 00:10:00.566
She said, "Do you know
why I'm looking at you?"

00:10:00.566 --> 00:10:02.067
I said, "Why are
you looking at me?"

00:10:02.067 --> 00:10:03.669
She said, "Because I remember
when my kids were that age."

00:10:03.669 --> 00:10:04.903
Hmm.

00:10:04.903 --> 00:10:05.704
I said, "Tell me
about your kids."

00:10:05.704 --> 00:10:06.939
"I have three sons."

00:10:06.939 --> 00:10:08.173 align:start size:84% position:16%
"How are they doing?
What do they do?"

00:10:08.173 --> 00:10:10.909
"One's a doctor,
one's an engineer,

00:10:10.909 --> 00:10:11.844
and one's a lawyer."

00:10:11.844 --> 00:10:13.011
"Really, all successful?"

00:10:13.011 --> 00:10:13.845
"All successful."

00:10:13.845 --> 00:10:14.680
"All married with kids."

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:15.781
"All married with kids."

00:10:15.781 --> 00:10:17.083
"Give me three secret sauce.

00:10:17.083 --> 00:10:18.017
What was it?"

00:10:18.017 --> 00:10:18.817
Said, "I'll only give you one."

00:10:18.817 --> 00:10:20.219
I said, "What's that?"

00:10:20.219 --> 00:10:23.989 align:start position:0%
She says, "If you ever threaten
to discipline your kids,

00:10:23.989 --> 00:10:25.024
follow through."

00:10:26.158 --> 00:10:27.926
I was, like, "Out of all
the advice you can give,

00:10:27.926 --> 00:10:29.194
you give me this?"

00:10:29.194 --> 00:10:31.430
If you threaten them,
always follow through

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:33.231
because your word
can't lose weight.

00:10:33.231 --> 00:10:34.266
- Yeah.

00:10:34.266 --> 00:10:35.101
- This is five years ago.

00:10:35.101 --> 00:10:36.369
I'm at Nordstrom's.

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:38.104 align:start size:84% position:16%
That lady was in my
life for five minutes.

00:10:38.104 --> 00:10:39.805
That impact is permanent.

00:10:39.805 --> 00:10:41.440 align:start size:84% position:16%
You got certain people
that are one day,

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:42.708
certain people that are a month,

00:10:42.708 --> 00:10:43.943
certain people that are year,

00:10:43.943 --> 00:10:45.511 align:start size:81% position:19%
certain people
that are a decade.

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:47.013
But if you think, like,

00:10:47.013 --> 00:10:48.581 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you have a relationship
with the man upstairs,

00:10:48.581 --> 00:10:50.716
and you say, "How did this
person come into my life?

00:10:50.716 --> 00:10:52.885
What is the chance of
me meeting this person?

00:10:52.885 --> 00:10:53.853
What?

00:10:53.853 --> 00:10:55.388
I'm the luckiest man alive.

00:10:55.388 --> 00:10:57.990
So when you look at it
from that perspective,

00:10:57.990 --> 00:10:59.592 align:start size:88% position:13%
and then now when I
wake up in the morning,

00:10:59.592 --> 00:11:01.360
at the beginning, you and
I were, you know, joking

00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:02.928 align:start size:84% position:16%
about poisoning the
drink, and I told you,

00:11:02.928 --> 00:11:04.964 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said, "If God
takes me today, man,

00:11:04.964 --> 00:11:06.465
I've lived the most
incredible life.

00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:08.067
I am so grateful.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:10.435
Everything from here
is dessert and bonus."

00:11:10.435 --> 00:11:14.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you know, that's a
brief element of the story

00:11:14.706 --> 00:11:16.041
I haven't told before.

00:11:16.041 --> 00:11:17.810 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Do you try to
acknowledge that every day?

00:11:17.810 --> 00:11:19.778 align:start size:88% position:13%
I sense that you do
from watching your show

00:11:19.778 --> 00:11:20.713
and just watching what
you're doing on Instagram

00:11:20.713 --> 00:11:22.314
'cause I've noticed for me,

00:11:22.314 --> 00:11:24.783
and maybe this is partly
just being a new father,

00:11:24.783 --> 00:11:27.987
like, I really am, like,
things have been good.

00:11:27.987 --> 00:11:29.555 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like, I don't want
anything else.

00:11:29.555 --> 00:11:30.756
It's good. It's really good.

00:11:30.756 --> 00:11:32.525
I'm doing what I'm
supposed to be doing.

00:11:32.525 --> 00:11:35.094 align:start size:84% position:16%
I have the family
I'm supposed to have.

00:11:35.094 --> 00:11:37.263 align:start size:88% position:13%
I'm, like, unbelievably
humbled by that.

00:11:37.263 --> 00:11:38.330
And I don't know
what to do with it-

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:39.432 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Yeah.
- sometimes in a way.

00:11:39.432 --> 00:11:41.367
- It's interesting you say that.

00:11:41.367 --> 00:11:44.670
So to me, this is the
battle I have, right,

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:47.406
because I have friends of
mine who made their money

00:11:47.406 --> 00:11:50.409
that no longer wanna work,
and they're living the life

00:11:50.409 --> 00:11:51.644
where it's like,
"Well, you know,

00:11:51.644 --> 00:11:53.179 align:start size:84% position:16%
Kobe had the father
time that came.

00:11:53.179 --> 00:11:55.481 align:start size:84% position:16%
You know, LeBron's
father time is coming.

00:11:55.481 --> 00:11:57.583
I'm kinda going through
the father time myself."

00:11:57.583 --> 00:11:58.951
People will say this, right?

00:12:00.119 --> 00:12:02.020 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I'll say, "Cool,
to each his own,

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:05.223
totally respect it, salute to
you," but I can't help myself.

00:12:05.223 --> 00:12:07.326
I tend to challenge
everybody around me,

00:12:07.326 --> 00:12:08.727
family, friends, kids.

00:12:08.727 --> 00:12:10.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
If you're around me,
you're either gonna like it

00:12:10.996 --> 00:12:12.231
'cause I'm gonna challenge you,

00:12:12.231 --> 00:12:14.432
or you're not gonna
like it, you know,

00:12:14.432 --> 00:12:15.934
'cause you, "This
is too much, man.

00:12:15.934 --> 00:12:17.903
I can't be around this guy too
much 'cause it's constantly,

00:12:17.903 --> 00:12:18.770
like, the next level
and the next thing."

00:12:18.770 --> 00:12:20.172
- [David] Yeah, yeah.

00:12:20.172 --> 00:12:21.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
- But you have to
realize, as tough as I am

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:26.411
on everybody else, I'm
a lot tougher on myself.

00:12:26.411 --> 00:12:29.381
The way I process this
is the following way.

00:12:30.515 --> 00:12:32.951
I'm greedy and selfish
in the following way.

00:12:32.951 --> 00:12:34.420
I watched a movie
"Meet Joe Black."

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:35.888
That completely messed me up.

00:12:35.888 --> 00:12:37.155 align:start size:84% position:16%
I've never seen the
movie "Meet Joe Black"

00:12:37.155 --> 00:12:39.058
till two months ago.
- Brad Pitt, right?

00:12:39.058 --> 00:12:40.559
But I don't think I've seen it.

00:12:40.559 --> 00:12:41.994 align:start size:97% position:3%
I don't think I've seen it.
- Oh, I mean, let me tell you,

00:12:41.994 --> 00:12:43.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
I can't tell you how
ridiculous this movie is.

00:12:43.262 --> 00:12:44.663 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Okay.
- The Vault Conference

00:12:44.663 --> 00:12:46.432 align:start size:81% position:19%
we held with Brady
two weeks ago-

00:12:46.432 --> 00:12:48.067
- Yeah, that was pretty awesome.

00:12:48.067 --> 00:12:50.035
- I talked about "Meet Joe
Black" for two, three days

00:12:50.035 --> 00:12:54.006
because the scene opens up
with Brad Pitt shows up,

00:12:54.006 --> 00:12:55.574
and Brad Pitt is death.

00:12:55.574 --> 00:12:57.209
I'm not gonna give you the
whole story, but he says,

00:12:57.209 --> 00:12:59.712 align:start size:88% position:13%
"I'm death," and he
keeps rubbing his chest,

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:01.346
you know, Anthony Hopkins,
one of the greatest actors

00:13:01.346 --> 00:13:03.548
of all time because he's
having a heart attack,

00:13:03.548 --> 00:13:05.650 align:start size:94% position:6%
and death comes and
says, "Your time is here.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:06.618
You're about to die."

00:13:06.618 --> 00:13:08.587
He's 65 years old.

00:13:08.587 --> 00:13:11.390 align:start size:97% position:3%
His oldest daughter is putting
together the big party.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.491
Presidents are showing up.

00:13:12.491 --> 00:13:13.425
Senators are showing up,

00:13:13.425 --> 00:13:14.660
Billionaires are showing up.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:16.161 align:start size:88% position:13%
And here's a businessman
that's a billionaire,

00:13:16.161 --> 00:13:18.430 align:start size:97% position:3%
gets in a helicopter from
Hamptons, goes to Manhattan,

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:20.900
does business, comes
back, and you know,

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:22.734
that's the life he's living.

00:13:22.734 --> 00:13:24.303
And he's so close
with his daughters.

00:13:24.303 --> 00:13:25.804
They love him.

00:13:25.804 --> 00:13:27.540
Youngest daughter's kinda,
like, his right-hand person

00:13:27.540 --> 00:13:29.474 align:start size:81% position:19%
that's doing stuff
with business.

00:13:29.474 --> 00:13:32.277
And she's dating the
other right-hand guy.

00:13:32.277 --> 00:13:36.549 align:start size:88% position:13%
And this house is,
like, a behemoth
60,000-square-foot house

00:13:36.549 --> 00:13:40.386
and impact, investments, board.

00:13:40.386 --> 00:13:41.453
And I'm watching this movie.

00:13:41.453 --> 00:13:44.323
I'm like, "Oh, my God,"

00:13:44.323 --> 00:13:47.326
fired me up because
it gave me urgency

00:13:47.326 --> 00:13:52.398
'cause my dream was always to
have the family live close.

00:13:53.198 --> 00:13:54.233
I want all my kids close to me.

00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:55.367
Obviously, they don't have to.

00:13:55.367 --> 00:13:56.735 align:start size:88% position:13%
They get to do
whatever they wanna do.

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:59.471 align:start size:81% position:19%
But I'm gonna bust
my tail to have

00:13:59.471 --> 00:14:01.973 align:start position:0%
so many different opportunities
where if you wanna be

00:14:01.973 --> 00:14:04.342
a realtor, you can manage
our real estate portfolio.

00:14:04.342 --> 00:14:06.111 align:start size:88% position:13%
If you wanna be a
lawyer, we need lawyers.

00:14:06.111 --> 00:14:07.880
If you wanna go do movies,
let's go fund your movies.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.214
If you wanna go be a teacher,

00:14:09.214 --> 00:14:10.616
let's build a school together.

00:14:10.616 --> 00:14:12.250 align:start size:97% position:3%
- They could be dog walkers
'cause I saw a video

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:13.752
that you did-
- Anything.

00:14:13.752 --> 00:14:14.887 align:start size:97% position:3%
- (laughing) where your kids
are now making some money

00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:16.121 align:start size:84% position:16%
dog walking.
- Yeah, dog walking.

00:14:16.121 --> 00:14:18.156
Any, you wanna be a
capitalist, go do it.

00:14:18.156 --> 00:14:21.527 align:start position:0%
But let's stay together because
I want us to stay together

00:14:21.527 --> 00:14:24.363
as a family, and I'm gonna do
my best to create that net.

00:14:24.363 --> 00:14:25.998
And then at the same
time, the other side,

00:14:25.998 --> 00:14:27.199
you know I wrote this book

00:14:27.199 --> 00:14:28.601 align:start size:84% position:16%
called "Choose Your
Enemies Wisely"

00:14:29.401 --> 00:14:30.536
that comes out December 5th.

00:14:30.536 --> 00:14:32.304
A lotta people say, you know,

00:14:32.304 --> 00:14:33.973
"Why choose your enemies wisely?

00:14:33.973 --> 00:14:35.341 align:start size:84% position:16%
Why not choose your
friends wisely?

00:14:35.341 --> 00:14:37.376 align:start size:84% position:16%
Why not choose your
allies wisely?"

00:14:37.376 --> 00:14:40.879
I really think this is a season

00:14:40.879 --> 00:14:44.616 align:start size:88% position:13%
where enemies are truly
formidable enemies

00:14:44.616 --> 00:14:48.721
that requires people who are
capable to fight to stand up.

00:14:48.721 --> 00:14:51.389 align:start size:84% position:16%
And I take that
role very seriously.

00:14:51.389 --> 00:14:53.925
I teach my kids, "If somebody
in school is getting bullied,

00:14:53.925 --> 00:14:56.095 align:start size:97% position:3%
and you can do something
about it, you gotta stop that.

00:14:56.095 --> 00:14:57.729
If you don't, you're a coward."

00:14:57.729 --> 00:15:00.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
So in a way, if I'm
teaching this to my kids,

00:15:00.933 --> 00:15:02.601
and I'm watching what's
going on in America,

00:15:02.601 --> 00:15:05.904 align:start position:0%
what's going on with, you
know, these guys telling Rumble

00:15:05.904 --> 00:15:07.272
what to do from
House of Commons,

00:15:07.272 --> 00:15:08.973
"Hey, you guys better
take this guy down,"

00:15:08.973 --> 00:15:12.378
and consider what YouTube did
to them from UK is telling

00:15:12.378 --> 00:15:14.846
Rumble, a Canadian
company based out of,

00:15:14.846 --> 00:15:16.315 align:start size:84% position:16%
who the hell are you
to say something?

00:15:16.315 --> 00:15:17.782
Or what they're
doing to parents,

00:15:17.782 --> 00:15:21.520
and you got 30 different cities
who are in Canada protesting

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.222
right now against
indoctrinating kids

00:15:24.222 --> 00:15:25.657 align:start size:88% position:13%
and have so much respect
