00:23:13.591 --> 00:23:15.359 align:start size:84% position:16%
This guy's a clinical
psychologist.

00:23:15.359 --> 00:23:17.996 align:start size:97% position:3%
So he spent most of his
life, he was teaching also,

00:23:17.996 --> 00:23:20.799
but spent most of his life
helping people get off drugs

00:23:20.799 --> 00:23:23.100
one on one like this, privately.

00:23:23.100 --> 00:23:25.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then, he becomes basically
the most famous person

00:23:25.937 --> 00:23:27.906
in the world overnight.

00:23:27.906 --> 00:23:32.077
And everywhere we went, we'd
get to airports in Sweden,

00:23:32.077 --> 00:23:33.979
and there'd be 200
people waiting for us

00:23:33.979 --> 00:23:35.847 align:start size:84% position:16%
because they got
their life in order.

00:23:35.847 --> 00:23:37.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he would talk to
every single one of them.

00:23:37.715 --> 00:23:40.318
I never saw the guy
be rude, or ignore,

00:23:40.318 --> 00:23:43.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
or walk away from
anybody, and it was, like-

00:23:43.121 --> 00:23:44.656 align:start size:97% position:3%
- But I will tell you this.
- Geez.

00:23:44.656 --> 00:23:46.524
- But I'll tell you this.

00:23:46.524 --> 00:23:50.728 align:start size:97% position:3%
I also will say he also
didn't know how to handle it.

00:23:50.728 --> 00:23:51.996 align:start size:84% position:16%
Hear me out.
- To an extent, yeah.

00:23:51.996 --> 00:23:53.698 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Hear me out.
- I was with him during that.

00:23:53.698 --> 00:23:57.102
- Yeah, so I remember, not
from the, you know, arrogant.

00:23:57.102 --> 00:23:58.336
I'm not talking

00:23:58.336 --> 00:23:59.871 align:start size:81% position:19%
that stuff at all.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:23:59.871 --> 00:24:02.774 align:start size:97% position:3%
- I'm talking about, you know,
one day, I'm having him on.

00:24:02.774 --> 00:24:04.042
And for about 30 minutes,

00:24:04.042 --> 00:24:06.477 align:start size:88% position:13%
he talked about how
much tweets bother him.

00:24:06.477 --> 00:24:07.779
- Yeah.

00:24:07.779 --> 00:24:09.047
- And he really didn't like

00:24:09.047 --> 00:24:10.481
what people were
saying on Twitter.

00:24:10.481 --> 00:24:12.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was kind of shocked
by him saying this.

00:24:12.383 --> 00:24:15.820
This is five years ago, first
time I had him on the show.

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.622
And then, I brought
him back at an event

00:24:17.622 --> 00:24:19.824
in 2019 at the Mirage.

00:24:19.824 --> 00:24:21.392
This is the event where
we had President Bush,

00:24:21.392 --> 00:24:22.827
Kobe Bryant, the
late Kobe Bryant.

00:24:22.827 --> 00:24:23.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is that event.
- I wanna talk about that.

00:24:23.995 --> 00:24:25.197
Yeah.

00:24:25.197 --> 00:24:26.298
- This is that event,
and he's speaking,

00:24:26.298 --> 00:24:28.200
and he's crying half the time.

00:24:29.501 --> 00:24:30.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "He's
going through something,"

00:24:30.768 --> 00:24:32.003
and I asked him a
couple questions.

00:24:32.003 --> 00:24:33.805
I'm like, "He's going
through something."

00:24:33.805 --> 00:24:35.339 align:start size:81% position:19%
That's the last
interview he does,

00:24:35.339 --> 00:24:37.775
and then he goes through the
phase that he went through,

00:24:37.775 --> 00:24:40.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he openly talked about
how he dealt with it,

00:24:40.879 --> 00:24:42.214
how challenging it was for him,

00:24:42.214 --> 00:24:45.050
and then the comeback
on what he's done,

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:47.185
and what his daughter's done.

00:24:47.185 --> 00:24:48.652
Both of them, I mean,

00:24:48.652 --> 00:24:51.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
and obviously, Jordan
Peterson is a powerhouse.

00:24:51.956 --> 00:24:54.225
He's a, you know,
force of nature.

00:24:54.225 --> 00:24:56.694
And he's duplicating
it with his daughter.

00:24:56.694 --> 00:24:58.796
And that's where
the respect goes,

00:24:58.796 --> 00:25:00.965
that your daughter is
carrying the torch.

00:25:00.965 --> 00:25:02.200
And I can only imagine

00:25:02.200 --> 00:25:03.301 align:start size:84% position:16%
where she's gonna
be later on in life.

00:25:03.301 --> 00:25:04.936
She's already crushing it.

00:25:04.936 --> 00:25:06.604
But imagine what that's
gonna be in 10 years.

00:25:06.604 --> 00:25:08.072
- So I wanna talk to you
about that Kobe thing.

00:25:08.072 --> 00:25:09.908
We talked about it one other
time when you were on the show,

00:25:09.908 --> 00:25:13.478 align:start size:84% position:16%
but so you basically
did the last big,

00:25:13.478 --> 00:25:14.746 align:start size:84% position:16%
was it the last
interview with Kobe?

00:25:14.746 --> 00:25:15.680
Or was it the last-
- It wasn't the last.

00:25:15.680 --> 00:25:16.815
- It was certainly the last big-

00:25:16.815 --> 00:25:17.948 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Right, yes.
- interview with Kobe.

00:25:17.948 --> 00:25:20.184
Kobe, we're both
basketball guys.

00:25:20.184 --> 00:25:21.453
We picked our top fives.

00:25:21.453 --> 00:25:22.687
I still think mine beats yours,

00:25:22.687 --> 00:25:24.422
but that's where
we do that later.

00:25:25.790 --> 00:25:28.759
But Kobe, I think maybe I
told you this privately.

00:25:28.759 --> 00:25:30.027
I can't remember.

00:25:30.027 --> 00:25:33.397
Two or three days before
he died, I was watching,

00:25:33.397 --> 00:25:35.800 align:start size:97% position:3%
I was just flicking the
channels, and I flicked past,

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.535 align:start size:88% position:13%
I lived in LA at the
time, and I flicked past

00:25:37.535 --> 00:25:40.304
Comcast Sports or whatever,
whatever the Lakers are on.

00:25:40.304 --> 00:25:41.739 align:start size:97% position:3%
And I saw Kobe, and I
hadn't seen him in a while.

00:25:41.739 --> 00:25:45.042 align:start size:97% position:3%
He had a beard, and he
looked like a million bucks.

00:25:45.042 --> 00:25:46.544 align:start size:97% position:3%
That was my thought, "He
looks like a million bucks."

00:25:46.544 --> 00:25:49.748
And I stopped, and I watched,
and just the way he spoke,

00:25:49.748 --> 00:25:51.282 align:start size:81% position:19%
that calmness that
he spoke with,

00:25:51.282 --> 00:25:53.518
and always licking his lips,
and, like, he was just ready

00:25:53.518 --> 00:25:56.955 align:start position:0%
to chew the world, and I
watched for about five minutes,

00:25:56.955 --> 00:25:58.656
and I swear to God this is true.

00:25:58.656 --> 00:26:00.058
I remember thinking,

00:26:00.058 --> 00:26:04.129
"This is a guy who
has done life right."

00:26:04.129 --> 00:26:06.163 align:start size:84% position:16%
That was either
the day or two days

00:26:06.163 --> 00:26:07.598 align:start size:84% position:16%
before he was dead.
(Pat exhaling)

00:26:07.598 --> 00:26:10.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, the day he
died, I saw it on Twitter.

00:26:10.302 --> 00:26:12.203
I immediately began to tear up.

00:26:12.203 --> 00:26:13.405
I was on tour with
Jordan at the time.

00:26:13.405 --> 00:26:15.539
I was about to get in an Uber.

00:26:15.539 --> 00:26:19.043
I get in the Uber, and it's a
young black guy as the driver.

00:26:19.043 --> 00:26:22.113
He's hysterical crying 'cause
he must have just found out

00:26:22.113 --> 00:26:24.215 align:start size:81% position:19%
at that moment,
hysterical crying.

00:26:24.215 --> 00:26:26.685 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said to him, "I know
it's Kobe, I know."

00:26:26.685 --> 00:26:29.120
And I was very early, so I said,

00:26:29.120 --> 00:26:30.388
"We don't have to go
anywhere for a while.

00:26:30.388 --> 00:26:31.790 align:start size:88% position:13%
You wanna just talk
about Kobe for a while?"

00:26:31.790 --> 00:26:33.291
And we spent about a half hour-

00:26:33.291 --> 00:26:34.158
- Get outta here.

00:26:34.158 --> 00:26:35.393 align:start size:75% position:25%
I swear to God-
- Wow.

00:26:35.393 --> 00:26:37.795
- just talking about
the 81-point game,

00:26:37.795 --> 00:26:39.998 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, the Denver game when
he flew in after the legal,

00:26:39.998 --> 00:26:42.133
like, everything, everything.

00:26:42.133 --> 00:26:46.270
And I remember thinking, like,
"Man, that guy, two days ago,

00:26:46.270 --> 00:26:49.073
I'm thinking he's
living the dream."

00:26:49.073 --> 00:26:51.276
Whatever the secret of the
universe is, he unlocked it.

00:26:51.276 --> 00:26:52.243
- Mm-hmm.

00:26:52.243 --> 00:26:53.478
(fingers snapping)

00:26:53.478 --> 00:26:54.745 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Gone like that,
and you sat with him

00:26:54.745 --> 00:26:56.948
and had, I think, one
of the best interviews

00:26:56.948 --> 00:26:58.182
that he's ever had.

00:26:58.182 --> 00:26:59.417
I don't even know
what my question is

00:26:59.417 --> 00:27:00.685
other than, what do
you do with that?

00:27:00.685 --> 00:27:02.152 align:start size:81% position:19%
What do you do
with that concept?

00:27:02.152 --> 00:27:06.992
- Yeah, you know, Kobe's
an August 23rd, 1978, baby.

00:27:07.792 --> 00:27:09.927
I'm an October 18th, 1978 baby.

00:27:09.927 --> 00:27:11.796
We're six weeks apart.
- Man, you guys are kids.

00:27:11.796 --> 00:27:12.764
I'm '76.

00:27:12.764 --> 00:27:13.798
Look at you.
- You're '76?

00:27:13.798 --> 00:27:15.133
But you look younger than me.

00:27:15.133 --> 00:27:16.367 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Yeah, it's-
- You look better than me.

00:27:16.367 --> 00:27:17.635 align:start size:84% position:16%
- It's the moisture
here in South Florida.

00:27:17.635 --> 00:27:19.170
(both laughing)

00:27:19.170 --> 00:27:22.407
- So when he came, and they
traded him for Vlade Divac-

00:27:22.407 --> 00:27:23.474 align:start size:84% position:16%
- Vlade Divac, yeah.
- Obviously,

00:27:23.474 --> 00:27:25.109
we were devastated.

00:27:25.109 --> 00:27:27.245
We didn't want lose
Vlade because Vlade's
a top-five center,

00:27:27.245 --> 00:27:28.446
greatest center of all time.

00:27:28.446 --> 00:27:30.081 align:start size:84% position:16%
- What, what?
- Hence the sarcasm.

00:27:30.081 --> 00:27:31.216
Hardcore sarcasm.
(David laughing)

00:27:31.216 --> 00:27:32.683
- Wow, you see,

00:27:32.683 --> 00:27:33.918
that didn't get by me.
- I'm glad you caught it.

00:27:33.918 --> 00:27:35.153 align:start size:84% position:16%
- (laughing) Come
on, top-five center.

00:27:35.153 --> 00:27:36.153 align:start size:81% position:19%
He was good. He
was a good passer.

00:27:36.153 --> 00:27:36.954
- I loved Vlade.
- Yeah, no, no.

00:27:36.954 --> 00:27:37.989
- But he's not Kobe.

00:27:37.989 --> 00:27:39.456 align:start size:72% position:28%
- Slow, yeah.
- I loved

00:27:39.456 --> 00:27:40.692 align:start size:97% position:3%
when he scored the points,
put his hands beyond his back.

00:27:40.692 --> 00:27:41.859
He went to Magic Johnson.

00:27:41.859 --> 00:27:43.261 align:start size:88% position:13%
I just love Vlade.
- I would've never lived

00:27:43.261 --> 00:27:44.429
that down if I had missed that.

00:27:44.429 --> 00:27:46.798 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Yeah. (laughs)
- That would've been...

00:27:46.798 --> 00:27:48.132
(David laughing)

00:27:48.132 --> 00:27:49.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So you know-
- Top-five Czechoslovakian

00:27:49.734 --> 00:27:51.802
or Yugoslavian, I guess.
- Yeah, and by the way,

00:27:51.802 --> 00:27:53.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think he's a GM or
something for Sacramento.

00:27:53.771 --> 00:27:56.473
I don't know if he still is or
not, but I like his swagger.

00:27:56.473 --> 00:27:58.142 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And those Sacramento teams
are awesome, different.

00:27:58.142 --> 00:28:00.644 align:start size:97% position:3%
- Yeah, phenomenal, him,
Christie, and all those guys,

00:28:00.644 --> 00:28:02.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
you know, Stojakovic,
great team.

00:28:02.480 --> 00:28:06.484
But you know, it was like,
"I'm gonna go to this place.

00:28:06.484 --> 00:28:07.419
I'm not an athlete.

00:28:07.419 --> 00:28:08.953
You're gonna go to this place.

00:28:08.953 --> 00:28:11.422
But listen, man, I'm gonna
bring the Mamba mentality

00:28:11.422 --> 00:28:14.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
in my own way in the
insurance space and boom.

00:28:14.591 --> 00:28:17.762
And then later on in 2019,
there's a video of me dressed

00:28:17.762 --> 00:28:21.099
as Doc from "Back
to the Future."

00:28:21.099 --> 00:28:22.300
- I don't think I've seen this.

00:28:22.300 --> 00:28:23.734
- And it's a video.

00:28:23.734 --> 00:28:26.003 align:start size:97% position:3%
I'll show it to you afterwards
'cause it's not public.

00:28:26.003 --> 00:28:29.507
And I'm saying one day, this
is 2011, I have Doc's hair.

00:28:29.507 --> 00:28:31.009
I'm wearing a whole thing.

00:28:31.009 --> 00:28:32.910
This event we're running,
I brought the DeLorean.

00:28:32.910 --> 00:28:35.012
I'm doing a whole skit
from stage with myself

00:28:35.012 --> 00:28:37.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a couple of our guys,
John, Fred, Terrance,

00:28:37.248 --> 00:28:38.183
and all these guys.

00:28:38.183 --> 00:28:39.317
We're doing what we're doing.

00:28:40.385 --> 00:28:42.119
And I said, "One day," 2011,

00:28:42.119 --> 00:28:43.721
I haven't even started
a YouTube channel yet.

00:28:43.721 --> 00:28:46.224
And I said, one day the
great Kobe Bryant will be

00:28:46.224 --> 00:28:47.958
on our show, and we'll
be having an interview,"

00:28:47.958 --> 00:28:49.160
and da, da, da, da, da.

00:28:49.160 --> 00:28:50.695
So that vision was cast,

00:28:50.695 --> 00:28:52.464
and eight years later,
Kobe's at the event.

00:28:52.464 --> 00:28:54.599 align:start size:84% position:16%
Our guys can't believe
this is happening.

00:28:55.433 --> 00:28:56.934
And he comes in.

00:28:56.934 --> 00:28:58.937
Hour and a half we spend in
a conference room together

00:28:58.937 --> 00:29:00.705
before he hits the stage.

00:29:00.705 --> 00:29:03.107
He talks to Dylan
for 15 minutes.

00:29:03.107 --> 00:29:05.677
Dylan at the time
was five years old.

00:29:05.677 --> 00:29:06.878
He talks to Jen for 15 minutes.

00:29:06.878 --> 00:29:08.880 align:start size:84% position:16%
They have the best
conversation together.

00:29:08.880 --> 00:29:11.082
Then, a 70-year-old woman,

00:29:11.082 --> 00:29:14.985
75-year-old woman comes in,
very nicely put together.

00:29:14.985 --> 00:29:17.488
And he runs up to her.

00:29:17.488 --> 00:29:20.124
They hug each other and they
have the nicest conversation

00:29:20.124 --> 00:29:21.859
where you can tell
the level of respect

00:29:21.859 --> 00:29:24.395 align:start size:97% position:3%
and love he has for her, and
I don't know who she was,

00:29:24.395 --> 00:29:28.632
but there was a certain
level of relationship

00:29:28.632 --> 00:29:29.901
towards each other.

00:29:29.901 --> 00:29:33.304
And he says, "So
Pat, do these types

00:29:33.304 --> 00:29:35.439
of interviews live
make you nervous?"

00:29:35.439 --> 00:29:36.708
I said, "Nah, I'm good."

00:29:36.708 --> 00:29:37.942
He says, "Ah, me neither.

00:29:37.942 --> 00:29:39.077
I've played in front
of 20,000 people."

00:29:39.077 --> 00:29:40.010
I said, "Nah, I totally get it.

00:29:40.010 --> 00:29:41.212
I mean, you're Kobe.

00:29:41.212 --> 00:29:43.314 align:start size:88% position:13%
I don't see you, but
I'm good at this point."

00:29:43.314 --> 00:29:44.482
Then, we hit the stage.

00:29:44.482 --> 00:29:45.917
A thousand people run up.

00:29:45.917 --> 00:29:47.418
We had to call the security.

00:29:47.418 --> 00:29:48.786
The benefit we had, because
the president was coming,

00:29:48.786 --> 00:29:50.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had 100 Secret Service.
(David laughing)

00:29:50.254 --> 00:29:52.623
So everything was pushing 'em
out, and then we sat down,

00:29:52.623 --> 00:29:54.959 align:start position:0%
we did the interview, and
obviously, the rest is history.

00:29:54.959 --> 00:29:56.327
But the day when he passed away,

00:29:56.327 --> 00:29:59.364
we were at Seasons 52
in Dallas, in Plano.

00:29:59.364 --> 00:30:02.032 align:start size:88% position:13%
And my phone says, "Kobe
Bryant, helicopter."

00:30:02.032 --> 00:30:02.867
Jennifer looks at CNN.

00:30:02.867 --> 00:30:04.836
We're like, "What?"

00:30:04.836 --> 00:30:06.471
Then, I go to ESPN. "What?"

00:30:06.471 --> 00:30:08.139 align:start position:0%
Twitter 'cause you know,
sometimes these hoax, you know,

00:30:08.139 --> 00:30:09.606 align:start size:97% position:3%
and this is not funny.
- And you can't believe it.

00:30:09.606 --> 00:30:10.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
You can't believe it.
- And then Dylan is like,

00:30:10.708 --> 00:30:12.476
"Wait, my friend, Kobe?"

00:30:12.476 --> 00:30:14.578
So yeah, I mean,
I was pretty wild.

00:30:14.578 --> 00:30:17.281
But you know what it is,
what you're saying here,

00:30:17.281 --> 00:30:18.549
that's the whole concept

00:30:18.549 --> 00:30:23.254
where you have to
enjoy the process,

00:30:23.254 --> 00:30:26.357
even when you're in
the grind, driving,

00:30:26.357 --> 00:30:29.260 align:start size:97% position:3%
to know that at any point this
can be taken away from you,

00:30:29.260 --> 00:30:31.162 align:start size:75% position:25%
- Yeah.
- just enjoy it

00:30:31.162 --> 00:30:33.598
because in some ways, people
take that message and say,

00:30:33.598 --> 00:30:35.066 align:start size:84% position:16%
"That's why I don't
work that hard.

00:30:35.066 --> 00:30:36.434
What's the purpose
of working that hard?

00:30:36.434 --> 00:30:38.036
If I know I'm gonna die one day,

00:30:38.036 --> 00:30:39.771
why am I doing all this stuff?"

00:30:39.771 --> 00:30:41.506 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's also not the
right way of thinking.

00:30:41.506 --> 00:30:44.309 align:start size:84% position:16%
I wanna work hard
with the people I love

00:30:44.309 --> 00:30:46.611 align:start size:84% position:16%
and using the talents
that God gave me.

00:30:46.611 --> 00:30:48.913 align:start size:88% position:13%
But if he takes me
today, I'm good as well

00:30:48.913 --> 00:30:50.181
because at the end of the day,

00:30:50.181 --> 00:30:52.050
you have no clue what
that day's going to be.

00:30:53.251 --> 00:30:54.819
- Do you consider
yourself political?

00:30:54.819 --> 00:30:57.021 align:start size:84% position:16%
'Cause we're crossing
paths now a lot,

00:30:57.021 --> 00:30:59.424
and the type of people
that are watching us are

00:30:59.424 --> 00:31:02.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
very similar in the
political sense of things.

00:31:02.126 --> 00:31:04.128
But I can never tell if
you really are political.

00:31:04.128 --> 00:31:05.530 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like, I saw you
